WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.980
RYAN JOHNSON: One of
the most important tests

00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:04.260
that we're going to do
is the breaching test.

00:00:12.127 --> 00:00:14.850
GIBBS KUGURU: Breaching is
sort of this ambush attack.

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.170
They need speed, power, stealth.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.750
RYAN JOHNSON: This is when we're
going to be able to measure

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.090
the color of the
great white shark

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.340
in its ultimate hunting mode.

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:33.865
NARRATOR: In the middle of
Mossel Bay sits Seal Island.

00:00:35.332 --> 00:00:37.040
RYAN JOHNSON: This
island's the epicenter

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:38.855
for great white sharks
in South Africa.

00:00:46.975 --> 00:00:54.700
NARRATOR: Every day, hundreds of
fur seals swim for their lives

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:57.158
through a gauntlet
of great whites.

00:00:57.158 --> 00:00:59.200
RYAN JOHNSON: The great
white sharks success rate

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.500
in hunting Cape fur
seals is almost 50%,

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:06.000
and that's really
high for any predator.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.150
So with these shocks I
got very specific areas

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.890
where they want to
hunt and patrol,

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:13.890
and it's usually right
underneath the natural routes

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:18.810
that the seals are exiting
and entering the islands.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.730
NARRATOR: Ryan and
Gibbs are towing

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:27.390
a decoy seal in the hopes of
encouraging sharks to breach.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.420
RYAN JOHNSON: It's about
trying to capture the breaching

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.660
shark alongside a
color board and being

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.970
able to measure the color
of that breaching shark.

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:43.460
NARRATOR: It's a quiet
morning, but Seal

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:47.290
Island rarely disappoints.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.780
GIBBS KUGURU: Oh,
there's a predation.

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:52.960
Natural predation
right over there.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.970
Oh, it's still going for it.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.930
Oh, [INTERPOSING VOICES]!

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:58.830
Oh.

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.025
Isn't this hot?

00:02:00.025 --> 00:02:01.400
RYAN JOHNSON: This
is in trouble.

00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:02.300
GIBBS KUGURU: Yeah.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.560
He's using the boat for cover.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.790
RYAN JOHNSON: And even
though the shark missed

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:07.340
on that first breach, it
scared that seal so much,

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:10.910
and it's now hiding around
the boat, using it for cover.

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:15.320
NARRATOR: The seal leads the
shark right to the decoy.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:16.978
MAN: Woo.

00:02:16.978 --> 00:02:20.240
GIBBS KUGURU: Oh, yes!

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.400
RYAN JOHNSON: Got it.

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.365
Got it.

00:02:22.365 --> 00:02:23.865
GIBBS KUGURU:
[INAUDIBLE] one there.

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:29.090
NARRATOR: The shark
and the color board

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.600
are clearly in frame.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:35.080
It's the first successful
breach of the experiment.

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:38.260
GIBBS KUGURU: It sends goose
bumps down my spine every time.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.580
I mean, you just can't help
but feel emotional every time

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.660
you see it.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.660
NARRATOR: Sharks
are here in numbers.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:47.560
GIBBS KUGURU: Oh.

00:02:47.560 --> 00:02:49.150
RYAN JOHNSON: There we go.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:58.218
NARRATOR: Stalking
seals all day long.

00:02:58.218 --> 00:02:59.760
GIBBS KUGURU: It's
having a go at it.

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.960
Woo.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:10.740
NARRATOR: As the sun sets
after a day of data collection,

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.325
the team hopes for
one last breach.

00:03:14.325 --> 00:03:15.570
RYAN JOHNSON: Hit that spot.

00:03:15.570 --> 00:03:16.470
Hit that spot.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.485
GIBBS KUGURU: Oh, ho.

00:03:23.485 --> 00:03:25.360
RYAN JOHNSON: Oh, we've
lost the color board.

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:27.745
We've lost the decoy.

00:03:27.745 --> 00:03:29.620
Because it's so dark,
the shark couldn't even

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.310
see which way to go.

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.310
He's going for it again.

00:03:41.050 --> 00:03:43.500
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

